+# Daily Grind components
+
+Framework-free Web Components used by the homepage. Load them once per page:
+
+```html
+<script type="module" src="/components/index.js"></script>
+```
+
+All three keep their content in light DOM (so it is crawlable, searchable and
+readable before JavaScript runs) and keep their markup, styles and behavior in
+an open shadow root. Theme them with the CSS custom properties listed in each
+file's header comment, or restyle specific internals with `::part()`.
+
+| Element | Purpose | Key API |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `<coffee-card>` | Menu item card: media, title, price/badge, actions, favorite toggle | `price`, `currency`, `badge`, `favorited`, `favoritechange` event, `:state(favorited)` |
+| `<brew-tabs>` | Tabs generated from child sections; roving tabindex, arrow keys, find-in-page aware | `label`, `selected` / `selectedIndex`, `change` event |
+| `<grind-disclosure>` | Styled native `<details>`; `group` makes a set mutually exclusive across shadow roots | `open`, `group`, `show()/hide()/toggle()`, `toggle` event |
+
+## Examples
+
+```html
+<coffee-card id="cold-brew" price="4.50" badge="New">
+  <img slot="media" src="cold-brew.jpg" alt="A glass of cold brew">
+  <h3 slot="title">Cold Brew</h3>
+  <p>Steeped for 18 hours.</p>
+  <a slot="actions" href="/menu/cold-brew" class="btn">View details<span class="visually-hidden"> about the Cold Brew</span></a>
+</coffee-card>
+
+<brew-tabs label="Brewing methods" selected="1">
+  <section data-label="Pour Over">…</section>
+  <section data-label="French Press">…</section>
+</brew-tabs>
+
+<grind-disclosure group="faq" open>
+  <h3 slot="summary">Do you offer decaf?</h3>
+  <p>Yes.</p>
+</grind-disclosure>
+```
+
+## Accessibility notes
+
+- Headings stay in the page (`<h3 slot="title">`), so the document outline is
+  controlled by the author, not the component.
+- `<brew-tabs>` renders tabs *and* panel wrappers inside its shadow root so
+  `aria-controls` / `aria-labelledby` ids resolve in one tree. Inactive panels
+  use `hidden="until-found"` where supported, so browser search and `#fragment`
+  links can still reach their content.
+- `<grind-disclosure>` wraps a real `<details>`; opening one member of a
+  `group` closes the others (native `name` grouping does not cross shadow roots).
+- Undefined elements fade in after two seconds (`:not(:defined)` rule in the
+  page CSS), so content is never hidden if the script fails to load.
